@methods: renter_housing
# The methods of the renter's housing stage as an addition to
# applications/housing-renting/declaration/stages/renter_housing/renter_housing.bl,
# rewritten from the earlier YAML file stages/renter_housing/methods.yml and the
# former block file methods/marginals_renter_housing.bl: the discrete choice over the rental
# quantities of XS on the policy builder; the derivative of the decision value
# in the wealth w_d, which enters cash one for one, from
# marginals_renter_housing.bl with its doc string; and the linear
# representation of the decision value and of its stated derivative, each
# named at its own Evaluation with a grid entry of its own, as the YAML names
# the two Evaluations by two entries (D4; D5, decided; writer's sheet §7).
#
# The policy builder gains no line, so its method is a file-level line routed
# by its path (rule 7; finding F24). The entry on dcsn_to_cntn, with on alone,
# binds nothing and is not written (writer's sheet §5).
#
# Each grid names the cash coordinate alone, as the YAML did: the income y_d,
# a level of the chain, takes the default (decision S7-C17 of 5 November 2026).
#
# The stage file is refused by the elaborator today (rule not-constructed, the
# definition XS := linspace(S_min, S_max, n_S) of its line 3), so no address of
# this file is checked against the stage's places until that set is
# constructed.
#
# The three settings the file reads are declared with their sets (writer's
# sheet §6): the bounds as points of ℝ₊, the set renter_housing.bl gives the
# wealth w_d, and the count in ℕ. The same two bounds are declared in ℝ₊₊ in
# the methods.bl of the two consumption stages, whose stage files give w_d
# that set.

w_points : ℕ       :: ["number of points of the cash grid"]
w_min : ℝ₊         :: ["lower bound of the cash grid"]
w_max : ℝ₊         :: ["upper bound of the cash grid"]

policy.method : !discrete_choice

[id=cntn_to_dcsn
    | evaluate[V].method : !Linear
    | evaluate[V].grid : !Cartesian(w_d=(w_min, w_max, w_points))
    | evaluate[D_{w_d}V].method : !Linear
    | evaluate[D_{w_d}V].grid : !Cartesian(w_d=(w_min, w_max, w_points))] {
    D_{w_d}V = D_{w_rent}V[>]    :: [id=marginal, "the derivative with respect to the wealth w_d brought into the stage, which enters cash one for one"]
}
